# Visit Sarva — Private Real Estate CRM Implementation Plan

This document outlines the strategy for transforming the existing Visit Sarva web application into a complete private internal Real Estate CRM. The primary objective is to implement an enterprise-grade, internal business management tool while preserving the existing public-facing property capabilities.

## User Review Required

> [!WARNING]
> **Existing Role Schema Update**
> The current `models.py` uses `UserRole = Literal["buyer", "seller", "admin"]`. 
> I will extend this to include internal employee roles: `"trainee", "executive", "team_lead", "bdo", "founder"`. Alternatively, we can create a separate `Employee` collection specifically for the CRM logic if we want to keep public users and employees completely segregated. I propose merging them into the existing users collection but using a specific role, or keeping an `employees` collection linked to auth. We will use a separate `Employee` model for cleaner separation. Please confirm if this is acceptable.

## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> 1. **Public vs. Internal App routing**: Should the CRM UI be built directly into the existing React app under a new namespace like `/crm/...` alongside the public pages, or should it replace the existing `/admin` dashboard entirely? The plan assumes it replaces the `/admin` with `/crm` or `/internal` routes but keeps the public buyer/seller app intact.
> 2. **Authentication Flow**: Do employees log in through the same `/login` endpoint, or should they have a dedicated `/crm/login` to ensure separation from normal buyers and sellers?

## Proposed Changes

### Backend - Database and Models

The CRM will utilize the existing MongoDB infrastructure but introduce numerous internal business models and robust RBAC (Role-Based Access Control).

#### [MODIFY] backend/models.py
- Add `EmployeeRole` Literal: `trainee, executive, team_lead, bdo, founder`.
- Add `Employee` schema (User ID, Role, Department, Manager, Status, etc.).
- Add `Lead` schema (Source, Status, Assigned To, Timeline tracking).
- Add `Customer` profile schema.
- Add `Requirement` schema (Buy/Sell, Budget, Location, Specs).
- Add `PropertyOwner`, `Broker`, `Deal`, `SiteVisit`, `Followup`, `Task`, `Document` schemas.
- Add `AuditLog` schema.

#### [NEW] backend/routers/crm_auth_router.py
- Add specific endpoints for employee authentication and robust session/token issuance.

#### [NEW] backend/routers/crm_*.py
- Create organized routers for each module:
  - `crm_leads.py`: Lead assignment, timeline updates.
  - `crm_properties.py`: Internal property tracking, rule-based matching.
  - `crm_deals.py`: Negotiations, commission tracking (restricted access).
  - `crm_tasks.py`: Follow-ups, site visits, assignments.
  - `crm_users.py`: Employee management (Founder/Admin only).

#### [NEW] backend/services/rbac_service.py
- Centralized permission service determining access dynamically based on `USER -> ROLE -> PERMISSION -> RESOURCE -> OWNERSHIP`.

#### [MODIFY] backend/server.py
- Mount new CRM routes securely.

